<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 13th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1200s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/13th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1250 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10357 5451" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1250 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="7559" cy="780" r="176"/><text x="7559" y="854" font-size="211">1</text></g><g><circle cx="5054" cy="728" r="176"/><text x="5054" y="802" font-size="211">2</text></g><g><circle cx="7846" cy="1933" r="176"/><text x="7846" y="2007" font-size="211">3</text></g><g><circle cx="6134" cy="1224" r="176"/><text x="6134" y="1298" font-size="211">4</text></g><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="176"/><text x="5709" y="1044" font-size="211">5</text></g><g><circle cx="6352" cy="637" r="176"/><text x="6352" y="711" font-size="211">6</text></g><g><circle cx="7018" cy="1385" r="176"/><text x="7018" y="1459" font-size="211">7</text></g><g><circle cx="4794" cy="1282" r="176"/><text x="4794" y="1356" font-size="211">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1250 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Delhi Sultanate &middot; Kingdom of France &middot; Byzantine Empire &middot; Almohad Caliphate &middot; Golden Horde &middot; Abbasid Caliphate &middot; Mongol Empire &middot; Khmer Empire</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Fourth Crusade</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Ain Jalut</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Saule</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Worringen</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of the Kalka River</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Genghis Khan</li><li>Marco Polo</li><li>Kublai Khan</li><li>Philip II of France</li><li>Louis IX of France</li><li>Thomas Aquinas</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1215–1294</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1162–1227</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1165–1223</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1225–1274</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1214–1270</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>1254–1324</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1200s, 357 recorded states were founded and 204 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Mongol Empire, the Kingdom of France and the Republic of Venice. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 13th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/13th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 13th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Mongol Empire <span>1206 CE – 1368 CE</span></li><li>Kingdom of France <span>987 CE – 1792 CE</span></li><li>Khmer Empire <span>802 CE – 1431 CE</span></li><li>Abbasid Caliphate <span>750 CE – 1517 CE</span></li><li>Byzantine Empire <span>330 CE – 1453 CE</span></li><li>Golden Horde <span>1242 CE – 1502 CE</span></li><li>Delhi Sultanate <span>1206 CE – 1526 CE</span></li><li>Almohad Caliphate <span>1121 CE – 1269 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Fourth Crusade <span>1204</span></li><li>Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa <span>1212</span></li><li>Battle of the Kalka River <span>1223</span></li><li>Battle of Saule <span>1236</span></li><li>Battle of Ain Jalut <span>1260</span></li><li>Battle of Worringen <span>1288</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Genghis Khan <span>2: c. 1162–1227</span></li><li>Marco Polo <span>6: 1254–1324</span></li><li>Kublai Khan <span>1: 1215–1294</span></li><li>Philip II of France <span>3: 1165–1223</span></li><li>Louis IX of France <span>5: 1214–1270</span></li><li>Thomas Aquinas <span>4: 1225–1274</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
